  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "What are the solutions of the equation $(x-2)^{2}=-49?$",
  "worked_solution": "The left-hand side is a perfect square. Therefore, we can solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =-49 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-49} \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 7\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =2\\pm 7\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=2+7\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=2-7\\,\\text{i}.$",
